# =============================================================================
# prod2 (columbinecoprod2) crontab — Energy Domain reports
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REFERENCE COPY for disaster recovery. cron does NOT read this file; the live
# crontab lives in root's cron spool. Keep this in sync with the live copy.
#
#   Restore after a rebuild:   crontab /root/energy-domain/deploy/prod2.crontab
#   Edit the live schedule:    crontab -e     (then update this file to match)
#   Show the live copy:        crontab -l
#
# NOT restored by this file (per-box, gitignored — recreate them separately):
#   * run.sh   — the wrapper each line calls (cd + start/end/exit logging)
#   * .env     — ED_* creds, GMAIL_USER/GMAIL_APP_PW, RIGS_EMAIL_TO=tad.jones,zoho
#
# Schedule semantics:
#   * Weekly rigs+permits -> tad.jones + zoho, Fridays 6:00 PM MT. Retries hourly
#     Fri evening + all Saturday if the Energy Domain API 503s. --once (week
#     period) sends only the first success; --friday pins DATE_PROD and the
#     permits 42-day window to the Friday, so a Saturday retry still produces the
#     Friday-dated report Zoho's weekly pivots expect. Recipients come from
#     RIGS_EMAIL_TO in .env (tad.jones + zoho).
#   * TEMP daily rigs -> tad.jones only (--to override), hourly 06:00-22:00 MT.
#     --once (day period) sends once/day. Remove when no longer wanted.
#
# All behavior is set via CLI flags (--email/--friday/--once/--period/--to) —
# no inline env vars — so the lines are portable and self-documenting.
# =============================================================================

# Energy Domain reports (rigs + permits) -> tad.jones + zoho, Fridays 6:00 PM MT
# --import-ready publishes data/ready/<report>_<friday>.json on full success (see deploy/Rigs_Permits_Generator.md)
0 18-23 * * 5 /root/energy-domain/run.sh rigs_ed.py    --email --friday --once rigs_weekly    --period week --import-ready >> /root/energy-domain/cron_rigs.log 2>&1
0 0-23  * * 6 /root/energy-domain/run.sh rigs_ed.py    --email --friday --once rigs_weekly    --period week --import-ready >> /root/energy-domain/cron_rigs.log 2>&1
0 18-23 * * 5 /root/energy-domain/run.sh permits_ed.py --email --friday --once permits_weekly --period week --import-ready >> /root/energy-domain/cron_permits.log 2>&1
0 0-23  * * 6 /root/energy-domain/run.sh permits_ed.py --email --friday --once permits_weekly --period week --import-ready >> /root/energy-domain/cron_permits.log 2>&1

# TEMP: daily personal rigs copy -> tad.jones only, 6:00 AM MT (remove later)
# no --import-ready: the daily copy is not imported into Zoho
0 6-22 * * * /root/energy-domain/run.sh rigs_ed.py --email --once rigs_daily --period day --to tad.jones@columbineco.com >> /root/energy-domain/cron_rigs_daily.log 2>&1
